WEBVTT

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.565
People, as company bureaucrat,

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:27.360
I will today be conducting
the annual performance review.

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:29.529
With a twist.

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.033
Oh, no. The firing tie.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.785
Correct. I will be evaluating each of you,

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.371
and the lowest-rated employee,
possibly Zoidberg,

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:40.790
will be fired at sundown. Zoidberg.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.877
Classic Hermes.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.547
Let the interviews begin.
Good luck, everybody but Zoidberg.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.550
My primary duties?

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.471
Well, I assist the Professor
in whatever important research

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.639
he happens to be engaged in.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:03.855
Uh, yes, sir, I will be sure
to snore that science lamp right away.

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:15.158
Now, Leela, couldn't we just fire
you and have Fry or Bender fly the ship?

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:18.328
Not if you stand on their
air hose much longer.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.579
Noted.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.045
My job?
Toilets 'n' boilers, boilers 'n' toilets.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:28.922
Plus that one boiling toilet.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:31.174
Fire me, iffen you dare.

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:39.474
Now, then, while many
of you do half-ass jobs

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:44.187
and the rest do jobs whose ass ratio
ranges from 42% to a mere 11%,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.982
only the most pathetically
useless employee will be fired today.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:50.193
And that employee is...

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.238
Hermes Conrad.

00:01:53.321 --> 00:01:54.447
- What?
- No way!

00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:55.615
Hermes, no!

00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:59.369
Yes. My performance review
proves the main drag on our profit

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.788
is the time
I waste on performance reviews.

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:05.458
But you can't fire yourself now.
We were just getting to know each other.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:07.794
I've already notified
the central bureaucracy.

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.630
They'll be here two seconds ago.

00:02:12.507 --> 00:02:14.467
I suppose you're here
to tell me to pack it in?

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.261
Only if you buy me dinner first.

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:21.099
I'm being fired.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.560
I don't think it's appropriate
to joke around like that.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.894
You're right, Hermes.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:28.565
Meet Mark 7-G,
the machine who's replacing you.

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:32.068
I'm Mark 7-G, the machine
who's replacing you.

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:35.030
Will you be conducting
an exit interview?

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:38.199
Well, I wouldn't say no
to a little friendly debriefing.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:44.956
Bureaucrat Conrad, you are ordered
to relieve yourself of duty.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.708
Sounds like a party.

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:51.171
Goodbye.

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:04.559
Well, this is it.

00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:08.563
But I want you to know working here
has been the experience of a lifetime.

00:03:08.646 --> 00:03:10.231
Off you go.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.529
- So, I hear you're a machine... Ow.
- Traitor!

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:19.199
My friend's ample tuchus
is barely out the door,

00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:21.701
and you're already schmoozing
up to his replacement?

00:03:21.785 --> 00:03:23.119
Um, Zoidberg?

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.829
I don't think Hermes really liked you.

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:28.041
In fact, he hated you more
than anyone ever hated anyone.

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:32.796
What, you mean the remarks and the hits?
That was just friend teasing.

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:34.756
- Oy.
- You don't understand.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.550
He was the only one
who cared enough to insult me.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.761
I insult you, you fat sack.

00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:44.099
Sure, when it's convenient.
But Hermes was always there for me.

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:48.395
And now he's gone,
thanks to you, Mr. Bigshot 7-G.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:53.149
I'll never see Hermes again.

00:03:56.152 --> 00:03:58.988
On the bright side,
I'll never see Zoidberg again.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:04.077
Oh, there, there, husband.
I made your favorite, curried goat.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.662
It better be spicy.

00:04:16.131 --> 00:04:18.008
Well played.

00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:21.052
Ows.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.183
Ah. Fire.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.895
It burns! It burns!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.442
Not bad. Needs a little hot sauce.

00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:41.865
I just don't know how we'll get by.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.868
Then I guess this wouldn't be a good time
to tell you that I'm pregnant.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.994
What?

00:04:46.077 --> 00:04:48.413
- And you're not the father.
- No!

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:51.708
I'm just joking, husband.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.711
See now? Things don't seem
so bad anymore, do they?

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.755
You're right. Thank you, LaBarbara.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.174
Oh, also, I wrecked the car.

00:05:00.592 --> 00:05:03.094
This here is a mugging!
Hand over your skin.

00:05:03.178 --> 00:05:05.930
My ebony splendor? Me don't think so.

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.308
I said hand it over. I'm hungry!

00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:13.813
For God's sake, woman,
just give him your skin!

00:05:13.897 --> 00:05:15.273
Can't you see he's crazy?

00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:18.777
You calling me crazy?

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.988
Ain't nothing crazy about me but my brain.
Right, brain?

00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:26.368
Right! No, not you, right brain.
Right, left brain? Right!

00:05:26.743 --> 00:05:28.370
Okay, then.

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.080
Do something, Hermes.

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:34.292
I can't! When I fight machinery,
machinery always wins!

00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:36.086
Freeze, bagwad.

00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:42.175
You're under arrest for
attempted epidermicide.

00:05:42.258 --> 00:05:45.679
I'm coming for you, man.
Ain't no jail can hold me.

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:49.349
That's why you're going straight
to the electromagnetic chair.

00:05:49.432 --> 00:05:53.019
And then I'm-a stab it.

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:04.864
Stop!
It's driving me sane!

00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:13.540
Hey, Bender,
you should become an executioner.

00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:15.875
You could kill humans
and wear a cool hood.

00:06:15.959 --> 00:06:18.253
Nah, I like my victims to know who did it.

00:06:18.278 --> 00:06:18.865
Psst.

00:06:19.235 --> 00:06:22.173
Hermes! Boy, am I indifferent to see you.

00:06:22.257 --> 00:06:24.884
We need to talk. Alone.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.970
Okay, Hermes. Sure.

00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:32.851
Fry, could you come in here

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:35.729
and help me rub on this
new scented body oil?

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:37.480
In a second. I'm eavesdropping.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.482
Please, Fry?

00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:41.609
Leela punishes me
when I don't use enough.

00:06:41.693 --> 00:06:43.361
I said not now!

00:06:43.445 --> 00:06:45.530
Sure, I know a guy.

00:06:54.956 --> 00:06:59.669
Yuri here runs the most sanitary
surgical implant parlor in Filthytown.

00:06:59.753 --> 00:07:03.923
So, I hear you're an expert in
the shadowy field of body augmentation.

00:07:04.007 --> 00:07:07.010
I am expert in shadowy field
of many things.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.179
I need something that'll make me
less inferior

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.890
to today's modern machinery.
Can you help me?

00:07:11.973 --> 00:07:14.434
No problem. I prepare operating room.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:22.150
Oh, honey, I'm home!

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:25.570
Pops?

00:07:25.653 --> 00:07:27.405
Is that a harpoon in your chest?

00:07:27.489 --> 00:07:29.824
Yes. And I'm happy to see you.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:34.245
Mm.

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:42.295
And the best part is,

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:45.799
the whole package fits neatly
in the space where my giblets used to be.

00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:50.095
I'm kind of a harpoon snob,
and let me say, that thing is gorgeous.

00:07:50.178 --> 00:07:52.597
But do you really need chest artillery?

00:07:52.681 --> 00:07:54.474
It's not just a weapon.

00:07:54.557 --> 00:07:57.268
It's the bureaucrat's best friend.
Observe.

00:07:57.352 --> 00:07:59.020
Oh, Mark 7-G?

00:07:59.104 --> 00:08:02.774
Would you mind fetching that carton
from the top shelf?

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:09.489
Pitiful and sickening.

00:08:09.572 --> 00:08:10.990
Okay, little man,

00:08:11.074 --> 00:08:13.660
let a professional bureaucrat
show you how it's done.

00:08:18.206 --> 00:08:19.958
My best wasn't good enough.

00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:22.252
I'll need my personnel file, please.

00:08:26.464 --> 00:08:30.010
Welcome back, old friend.
I missed you terribly.

00:08:30.093 --> 00:08:33.263
You do everything terribly.
And I'm not your friend.

00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:37.017
Good old Hermes.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.811
When he stops insulting,
that's when I worry.

00:08:39.894 --> 00:08:41.104
Oh, dear!

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:44.858
I was leaning over the sink
eating pureed clams

00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:47.569
when my teeth fell in the disposal.

00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:50.822
Scruffy, could you retrieve them?

00:08:50.905 --> 00:08:53.742
'Taint a boiler nor a toilet. Pass.

00:08:53.825 --> 00:08:56.244
I'll fetch my hand tools.

00:08:56.327 --> 00:09:00.081
Hand tools? Why don't you get an
extendo-arm implant, like mine?

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.503
Oh, no. No more implants.

00:09:05.587 --> 00:09:08.381
I don't want to end up a cold,
emotionless machine like you.

00:09:08.465 --> 00:09:09.716
That's sweet, Hermes.

00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:12.469
Maybe I should get an extendo-arm.

00:09:19.351 --> 00:09:21.811
How long will it take to
install an extendo-arm?

00:09:21.895 --> 00:09:24.397
I have golf game in half-hour, so

00:09:24.481 --> 00:09:25.523
half-hour.

00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:35.241
Thank you, Hermes.

00:09:35.325 --> 00:09:38.119
I don't know.
It seems like a lot of trouble

00:09:38.203 --> 00:09:40.163
to cut off your arm just to snake a drain.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.082
It's not just a drain snake.

00:09:42.165 --> 00:09:44.751
It comes with a set
of interchangeable accessories.

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.169
Jackhammer,

00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:50.256
vegetable peeler, pipe-bending jig.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.592
A machine that can bend? No way.

00:09:52.676 --> 00:09:56.888
But, Hermes, old friend, didn't you say
you were through with the implants?

00:09:56.971 --> 00:09:59.015
Oh, don't be such a spoilsport.

00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:01.393
Such a mild insult.

00:10:01.476 --> 00:10:04.020
That's not my Hermes. Speaking of,

00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:06.856
what happened to your
cut-off body parts, anyhow?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.149
Right here.

00:10:09.192 --> 00:10:11.361
I was going to donate them
to the Salvation Air Force,

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:13.113
but they're starting to rot.

00:10:13.196 --> 00:10:17.200
Then I'll just take them and,
throw them away, shall I, why not?

00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:29.379
So, friend, welcome to my home.
I'm very proud of it.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.715
But I want to hear what you think.

00:10:32.048 --> 00:10:35.093
"Oh, mon, I'm Hermes,
and I think it stinks in here

00:10:35.176 --> 00:10:38.304
"like a green snake,
or something else that's Jamaican."

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:41.891
Good one at my expense, Hermes.

00:10:46.396 --> 00:10:49.149
Well, I must admit it's not bad.

00:10:49.232 --> 00:10:52.569
And it will cut two or three hours a day
off my cornrowing routine.

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:55.363
Yes, our lives will never be the same.

00:10:56.406 --> 00:10:58.408
Darn it! I'll be right back.

00:11:04.039 --> 00:11:09.002
Hermes, oh, you foolish man,
what do you need a Cylon eye for?

00:11:09.085 --> 00:11:10.920
Now, calm down, dear.

00:11:11.004 --> 00:11:14.424
You know, you look
even hotter in infrared.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:25.226
Husband, some things were
not meant to be cylonned.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:28.396
Now, you must promise me
you won't be getting any more upgrades.

00:11:28.773 --> 00:11:30.149
I promise.

00:11:36.488 --> 00:11:37.655
Wow.

00:11:44.954 --> 00:11:47.832
Nice shiny metal ass, Hermes.

00:11:50.001 --> 00:11:54.422
So, with all these implants, what exactly
is the difference between you and a robot?

00:11:54.506 --> 00:11:57.592
I still have one thing
no robot shall ever have.

00:11:57.676 --> 00:12:01.096
A good old flesh-and-blood human brain.

00:12:01.179 --> 00:12:03.139
Yes, a big, smart brain.

00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:06.101
Not like dum-dum Zoidberg,
right, Hermes? Right?

00:12:06.184 --> 00:12:09.521
Mecha-Hermes has no interest
in such nonsense.

00:12:14.192 --> 00:12:18.321
Uh, Mr. Conrad, did you remember
to save the trimmings for me?

00:12:18.405 --> 00:12:20.365
Yes, yes, Doctor. Right here.

00:12:24.327 --> 00:12:27.622
Wait. You're not eating my
discarded flesh, are you?

00:12:27.706 --> 00:12:29.833
How could you even ask such a thing?

00:12:29.916 --> 00:12:33.128
Of course I tried eating you,
but your flesh was too spicy.

00:12:33.211 --> 00:12:36.131
Thanks to years of LaBarbara's
curried goat, no doubt.

00:12:36.214 --> 00:12:38.967
But my mecha-stomach
has no need of goat.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.970
Mecha-Hermes has spoken!

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.973
Mecha-Hermes still wants to know
what you're doing with his pieces.

00:12:45.056 --> 00:12:47.892
Something wonderful.

00:12:49.561 --> 00:12:52.981
Give it way up
for Dr. Zoidberg and little Hermes.

00:12:54.691 --> 00:12:56.026
Hello. Hello.

00:12:58.319 --> 00:13:02.073
So, little Hermes,
did you hear I've taken up running?

00:13:02.157 --> 00:13:05.744
"Yeah, from restaurant to restaurant.
Ho-ho, mon."

00:13:08.997 --> 00:13:11.458
"Seriously, though, have you lost weight?"

00:13:11.541 --> 00:13:12.584
Yes.

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.337
"Looks like you found it again."

00:13:17.756 --> 00:13:21.092
Oh, boy.
That was quite a zinger, old friend.

00:13:21.176 --> 00:13:22.260
"I'm not your friend.

00:13:22.344 --> 00:13:25.221
"I'm out of here the second
you let go of my bowels."

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.934
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.
I'll be here all week.

00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:32.062
"You've been warned, people."

00:13:32.896 --> 00:13:34.147
He's good.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:37.025
I can only see one of his
four mouth tendrils moving.

00:13:37.108 --> 00:13:39.736
"So, Mr. Conrad, did you enjoy the show?"

00:13:39.819 --> 00:13:41.237
Alas, no.

00:13:41.321 --> 00:13:44.491
Seeing what I once was
filled me with regret.

00:13:44.574 --> 00:13:46.826
You could always undo your implants.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:49.412
Regret that I still have one human part.

00:13:49.496 --> 00:13:54.918
That meat puppet disgusts me.
It's time for the ultimate upgrade.

00:13:55.001 --> 00:13:57.587
But the only thing you
haven't upgraded is your brain.

00:13:57.671 --> 00:13:59.047
Exactly.

00:14:01.299 --> 00:14:02.509
Oops.

00:14:04.094 --> 00:14:08.932
Robot brain implant? Never.
No one in right mind would do that.

00:14:21.653 --> 00:14:23.947
A freshly dug robot grave.

00:14:24.531 --> 00:14:26.324
Let's exhume-a-zoom-zoom.

00:14:26.408 --> 00:14:27.951
Step aside.

00:14:34.999 --> 00:14:37.460
Bing-reka! The brain circuit.

00:14:37.544 --> 00:14:40.422
Come, fellows.
Let's go home and install it.

00:14:40.505 --> 00:14:45.427
Enjoy eternity without your brain,
anonymous dead robot.

00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:03.862
So, little Hermes, are you ready
to watch some brain surgery?

00:15:03.945 --> 00:15:07.198
"I'm ready to shoot myself
if it'll get me off your lap."

00:15:09.451 --> 00:15:13.830
Open the dome
and unleash the power of the heavens!

00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:29.971
Ah, now I can see what I'm doing.
Commence the operation!

00:15:32.474 --> 00:15:34.768
Terminate the operation.

00:15:34.851 --> 00:15:36.436
LaBarbara? Dwight?

00:15:36.519 --> 00:15:39.230
I just got an urgent text
from little Hermes.

00:15:39.314 --> 00:15:43.109
You can't do this thing.
You don't even know whose brain that is.

00:15:43.193 --> 00:15:44.361
It doesn't matter.

00:15:44.486 --> 00:15:47.864
Any robot brain will improve my fitness
as a husband and father.

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:52.494
You can't be a husband and father
if you don't have a wife and son.

00:15:52.577 --> 00:15:53.703
Wait.

00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:56.414
I care about you too much to lose you.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.835
But my new robot brain won't.
Commence the operation.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:04.923
Well you'll have to commence it
without me, Hermes.

00:16:05.006 --> 00:16:06.883
And commence living without me.

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:09.844
Because I will commence
divorce proceedings.

00:16:09.928 --> 00:16:12.514
Oh, I hope to God
I'm using that word correctly.

00:16:15.725 --> 00:16:18.186
Oh, I can't do this, Hermes.

00:16:18.353 --> 00:16:20.897
Your wife's moving plea
has made me realize

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.191
you might have litigious survivors.

00:16:23.274 --> 00:16:24.901
Oh, thank you, Professor.

00:16:24.984 --> 00:16:26.069
Come now.

00:16:26.152 --> 00:16:28.530
Let's go try that Korean noodle place
you were telling me about.

00:16:30.365 --> 00:16:34.369
There will be no noodles
until the operation is complete.

00:16:41.001 --> 00:16:42.961
You can't force me to operate.

00:16:43.044 --> 00:16:45.880
Maybe not, but perhaps
I can encourage you

00:16:45.964 --> 00:16:47.882
with my encouragement drill.

00:16:52.262 --> 00:16:54.639
Wait. I'll perform the surgery.

00:16:54.723 --> 00:16:57.100
You? With those clumsy claws?

00:16:57.183 --> 00:16:58.268
It's true, old friend.

00:16:58.351 --> 00:17:01.146
My claws are too clumsy
for such delicate work.

00:17:02.313 --> 00:17:04.107
"But mine aren't.

00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:07.944
"You, mon, give me that robot brain."

00:17:08.028 --> 00:17:10.280
And you, metal guy, lie down.

00:17:10.363 --> 00:17:13.616
Zoidberg, this makes no sense.
Why are you helping him?

00:17:13.742 --> 00:17:15.201
And what's that catchy beat?

00:17:15.285 --> 00:17:16.870
I'll tell you. Two, three...

00:17:16.953 --> 00:17:20.248
I was lonesome for my friend
a minute ago

00:17:20.331 --> 00:17:24.044
When a happy thought
dispelled my woe

00:17:24.127 --> 00:17:27.172
And I felt perhaps he'd be
a bit less dull

00:17:27.255 --> 00:17:30.383
"If I sliced up his cyborg skull"

00:17:30.467 --> 00:17:31.843
He wants a brain

00:17:31.926 --> 00:17:33.803
He wants a robot brain

00:17:33.887 --> 00:17:35.138
Another brain

00:17:35.472 --> 00:17:37.557
Let's see if he feels pain

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.892
A brand-new brain

00:17:38.975 --> 00:17:40.894
It might drive him insane

00:17:40.977 --> 00:17:42.479
He wants a brain

00:17:42.562 --> 00:17:44.397
He wants a robot brain

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.780
Does anyone else find it freaky

00:17:51.863 --> 00:17:54.407
that Zoidberg is singing
harmony with himself?

00:17:54.491 --> 00:17:56.076
Oh, loosen up, Amy.

00:17:56.159 --> 00:17:58.453
My condolences, LaBarbara.

00:17:58.536 --> 00:18:00.330
I hope you find some comfort

00:18:00.413 --> 00:18:03.541
in staring at this throbbing
mass of nerve tissue.

00:18:03.666 --> 00:18:06.294
Oh, he's gone!

00:18:06.378 --> 00:18:08.672
Oh, Zoidberg, what have you done?

00:18:08.838 --> 00:18:12.801
I'll tell you what I've done.
I've brought your husband back.

00:18:24.062 --> 00:18:25.647
Pops.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:28.233
Sweet reawakenin' of me, a Jamaican-in.

00:18:28.316 --> 00:18:29.984
Hermes, you're alive.

00:18:30.068 --> 00:18:31.903
And practically rhyming.

00:18:32.862 --> 00:18:35.990
Wife, Son, I am so sorry.

00:18:36.074 --> 00:18:39.411
Once I started upgrading myself,
I lost all control.

00:18:39.494 --> 00:18:40.912
But I see now

00:18:40.995 --> 00:18:43.957
that if you can't be man enough
with your own parts,

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.251
no amount of machinery will help.

00:18:50.714 --> 00:18:52.424
Not so fast.

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:55.719
But faster than that!

00:19:01.891 --> 00:19:04.436
It's that insane robot, Roberto.

00:19:06.563 --> 00:19:10.817
- Quick, Hermes, the keys.
- I left them in my other body.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.027
Oh, yeah.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:15.989
And I'm-a stick them in your pancreas
till I find one that opens it.

00:19:26.708 --> 00:19:28.043
)

00:19:28.126 --> 00:19:32.255
I'm gonna peel off your skin
and eat it like pencil shavings.

00:19:33.882 --> 00:19:37.218
Ow. Thank God Zoidberg
didn't reattach my nerves.

00:19:40.472 --> 00:19:43.141
That's tasty. Too tasty.

00:19:45.101 --> 00:19:48.271
It burns. It... It burns!

00:19:48.813 --> 00:19:49.939
What's happening?

00:19:50.023 --> 00:19:51.441
The spicy curried goat.

00:19:51.524 --> 00:19:55.904
Hermes' skin is so saturated with it
that it's dissolving the bad robot.

00:20:00.408 --> 00:20:02.744
In the end, all his implants

00:20:02.827 --> 00:20:05.413
were no match for my wife's
reckless seasoning.

00:20:05.497 --> 00:20:08.249
Now, husband, don't you
think you owe Zoidberg

00:20:08.333 --> 00:20:10.960
a thank-you for saving you from yourself?

00:20:12.379 --> 00:20:13.546
But I hate him.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.965
Honey, we all do. But fair is fair.

00:20:18.885 --> 00:20:22.889
Zoidberg, I...
I know we have never been friends,

00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:25.558
but I appreciate what you did.

00:20:26.184 --> 00:20:27.602
Thank you.

00:20:28.269 --> 00:20:30.397
Never been friends?

00:20:31.815 --> 00:20:33.566
Ouch! What a zinger.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:36.861
Well, here's one for you,
Mr. Not-my-friend Conrad.

00:20:36.945 --> 00:20:39.572
You acted like a big jerk.

00:20:39.698 --> 00:20:41.991
You were selfish and stupid,
and you don't deserve

00:20:42.075 --> 00:20:44.828
a wife like LaBarbara or a friend like me.

00:20:44.953 --> 00:20:48.748
It's funny because it's mean.

00:20:48.832 --> 00:20:52.335
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.
I'll be here forever.

00:20:57.465 --> 00:20:58.842
He's doing it again.